title Fold T -- graft_promised_reach, and the fold that widened a family whole
prompt Autonomous loop -- Kyri voice and Radiant Style first, then REMEMBER and the itineraries, Standfast on reds, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, read one council-rota doc, sweep the prose Radiant, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every row in crux/REDS.md through %110 reads closed or released, so no red preempts this lap and the constructive queue is open.
think The running thread is the Caravan fold arc. Fold S's recommend named graft_promised_reach the better crux over provision_notes -- forty-two rungs against twenty-four -- and the carry meter, run fresh rather than recited, agreed: 42 rungs x 43 lines = 1763 carried, second in the printed queue.
think Council rota, lap index 1510 mod 27 + 1 = 26 -- active-designing/20260812-171050_the-1024-round-itinerary.md. Its filling law reads straight onto this lap: Lindy-first orders the constructive queue, reds preempt across any boundary, and a round is one keystone witnessed and sent. A fold is exactly that unit.
think Hash the family before folding it, as folds R and S taught. All forty-two came back one text at forty-three lines -- no absentee, no tier-owner standing apart. Three laps running had each found a rung the queue could not see; this lap found none, which is the discipline reporting a clean family rather than a discipline that stopped paying.
think Six symbols needed widening. Four of them -- word_at, read_count, read_words, already_holds -- are themselves fold families standing in forty-five rungs where this body stands in forty-two. The carry meter compares bodies by exact text, so pub is part of the text: widening forty-two and leaving three private would split each family in two.
think So the fold widened past its own family's edge, every rung that declares each symbol, forty-five apiece for the four bodies and forty-seven and fifty-eight for the two imports. 285 widenings, and no family split.
obs A fold pays its successors, and it pays them best by never handing them a split. Fold P cost nothing because fold O had widened exactly its five symbols one lap earlier. This lap reads that ledger from the other side -- the cheapest thing a fold can do for the folds after it is to widen wherever the symbol's family is wider than the body's, rather than stopping at its own edge.
obs The callee joined its caller. stand_taking_and_returning_reach lifted into the harness at fold L and reaches rung.graft_promised_reach on its sixth line; both bodies now stand in ladder_checks.rye, and the outward loop the harness prose describes turns one tier deeper.
obs One honest wobble, named rather than booked. The first choir run after the edit went RED on tools/caravan_inflight_witness.rish; that witness then ran GREEN standalone three times and GREEN inside a second full choir run. Its checks read a built binary, so a cold tree mid-rebuild is the likely cause, yet the cause is unproven. Recorded here so a second firing becomes a loom rather than a shrug (reds-first: a lantern that fires twice should become a loom).
